  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The materials to be used in the construction of the development hereby permitted shall be as shown on the approved drawings and supporting information listed in Condition 3.",
    "Condition : 3 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted (Design and Access Statement (revised) [received 19/01/2021]; Arboricultural Method Statement [received 07/01/2020]; Drainage Assessment Form [received 16/12/2020]; Drawings 2723(Rev.2), 2916(Rev.0), 2977(Rev.0), 2986(Rev.0), Existing Drainage plan, Flood Risk and Rainfall maps/data, Geotechnical Survey Report, Location Plan and Rocks Lane Brochure [received 10/12/2020]) therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 4 - In line with the hereby approved Tree Survey and Arboricultural Method Statement, prior to the works, tree protection barriers shall be installed and retained for the entire period of the duration of any works at the site; and prior to the completion a new London Plane tree (Platanus x hispanica) shall be planted and shall comply with the requirements specified in BS 3936 (1992) 'Specification of Nursery Stock Part 1 Trees and Shrubs', and in BS 4428 (1989) 'Recommendations for General Landscape Operations'. The new tree planted shall not be lopped or topped within a period of five years from the completion of the development. If new tree, within a period of five years from the completion of the development die, are removed, or become seriously damaged or diseased shall be replaced in the next planting season."
  ],
